(573237, 58358, 772, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EddyG:</b></div><hr/><i> For the record, I disagree with jmsetzler. When voting, how do you know that the submitter didn''t actually airbrush a shadow on to a wall and then set up the shot and take a picture? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>It''s easy if you look at the photograph...  look at the photograph...  look at the photograph :)  It''s not hard to do :)<br/> <br/>Yup.. the photographer could have done this, but not in this photograph :)</td>', 'Originally posted by EddyG: For the record, I disagree with jmsetzler. When voting, how do you know that the submitter didn''t actually airbrush a shadow on to a wall and then set up the shot and take a picture?   It''s easy if you look at the photograph...  look at the photograph...  look at the photograph :)  It''s not hard to do :) Yup.. the photographer could have done this, but not in this photograph :)', '2004-02-09 10:09:19.000000', NULL, 0),
