(577201, 58366, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/><b>The message</b> <br/>I get the impression from the title that this photo is intended to tell some story, like a hand touching wet paint. But to me it is more of a study in how shadows are affected by the form of the surface on which they appear.<br/> <br/><b>Creative choices</b> <br/>The composition is great. Just enough of the stairway is shown to let the viewer know what it is, and other shadows parallel the arm shadow which adds interest. Including the elbow in the arm shadow is effective. The square format works well for this image. The stairway itself isn''t really very interesting, and its shape is distorted by the wide angle focal length used here.<br/> <br/><b>Technical aspects</b> <br/>Focus is great. Exposure is a bit dark--not dark enough to be a low key photo (an approach that might have worked here to sinister effect), just enough to make me wonder why. Some Levels adjustment would make it look more natural as well as boosting the contrast of the shadow with the background. The shadow of the arm is too blurry, caused I think by a combination of motion blur and a large light source.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club!  The message I get the impression from the title that this photo is intended to tell some story, like a hand touching wet paint. But to me it is more of a study in how shadows are affected by the form of the surface on which they appear. Creative choices The composition is great. Just enough of the stairway is shown to let the viewer know what it is, and other shadows parallel the arm shadow which adds interest. Including the elbow in the arm shadow is effective. The square format works well for this image. The stairway itself isn''t really very interesting, and its shape is distorted by the wide angle focal length used here. Technical aspects Focus is great. Exposure is a bit dark--not dark enough to be a low key photo (an approach that might have worked here to sinister effect), just enough to make me wonder why. Some Levels adjustment would make it look more natural as well as boosting the contrast of the shadow with the background. The shadow of the arm is too blurry, caused I think by a combination of motion blur and a large light source.', '2004-02-11 21:29:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(578178, 58355, 11793, '<td valign="top">i too looked long at this image - and didnt think it was a photo.<br/> <br/>oh well - cool idea anyway - the 300d''s pulling up the rear with the shadows challenge ;}  mine placed quite low....</td>', 'i too looked long at this image - and didnt think it was a photo. oh well - cool idea anyway - the 300d''s pulling up the rear with the shadows challenge ;}  mine placed quite low....', '2004-02-12 16:10:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(578469, 58367, 16703, '<td valign="top">thanks to all who commented... i appreciate everyboy''s input...thanks again..</td>', 'thanks to all who commented... i appreciate everyboy''s input...thanks again..', '2004-02-12 20:16:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(578675, 58290, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetinigs from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/><b>The message</b> <br/>The artificial colors and soft focus give this image an ethereal feel, which is fitting for a shadow. It''s an interesting idea, and it does grab attention to begin with; unfortunately, there isn''t a lot of substance to hold it for long.<br/> <br/><b>Creative choices</b> <br/>The colors used here are well chosen, and keeping the trees black gives the image a grounding in reality. The texture of the snow is very nice. The composition isn''t very effective; the image is divided in half with little to connect the top and bottom halves. Cropping off the top part right below the largest tree would avoid this.<br/> <br/><b>Technical aspects</b> <br/>The focus is appropriately soft. The exposure seems right, but I think making the midtones a little darker would show the shadow better and improve the image.</td>', 'Greetinigs from the Critique Club  The message The artificial colors and soft focus give this image an ethereal feel, which is fitting for a shadow. It''s an interesting idea, and it does grab attention to begin with; unfortunately, there isn''t a lot of substance to hold it for long. Creative choices The colors used here are well chosen, and keeping the trees black gives the image a grounding in reality. The texture of the snow is very nice. The composition isn''t very effective; the image is divided in half with little to connect the top and bottom halves. Cropping off the top part right below the largest tree would avoid this. Technical aspects The focus is appropriately soft. The exposure seems right, but I think making the midtones a little darker would show the shadow better and improve the image.', '2004-02-12 23:40:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(578998, 58367, 8987, '<td valign="top">interesting and creative shot! cool :)</td>', 'interesting and creative shot! cool :)', '2004-02-13 06:55:36.000000', NULL, 0),
