(580034, 58214, 6624, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club:<br/>This is a clever response and a fitting one for the challenge.  My initial response was that it looked more like a shadow picture of a rabbit than a peace sign but that''s unimportant, really.  The watch face is too dark to really see the hands and the watch overall is out of focus or soft enough enough to be distracting.  There are many good suggestions below for re-shooting this so that the watch appears to go around the wrist.  Your concept was original and your underlying motive to be praised, the image is an interesting one.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club:This is a clever response and a fitting one for the challenge.  My initial response was that it looked more like a shadow picture of a rabbit than a peace sign but that''s unimportant, really.  The watch face is too dark to really see the hands and the watch overall is out of focus or soft enough enough to be distracting.  There are many good suggestions below for re-shooting this so that the watch appears to go around the wrist.  Your concept was original and your underlying motive to be praised, the image is an interesting one.', '2004-02-14 17:31:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(580364, 58390, 9906, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>With no photographers comments, I am not sure what you were attempting to achieve with this photo.<br/> <br/>I will say that this shot seems to suffer from a lack of focal point, both technically (nothing in focus) and compositionaly (too many distractions) however, I don''t really know what you were attempting to convey with this image.<br/>TC</td>', 'From the Critique Club With no photographers comments, I am not sure what you were attempting to achieve with this photo. I will say that this shot seems to suffer from a lack of focal point, both technically (nothing in focus) and compositionaly (too many distractions) however, I don''t really know what you were attempting to convey with this image.TC', '2004-02-15 04:38:20.000000', NULL, 0),
